      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PAID IN GLORY (3) showed little early speed at her last couple, the latest finishing fourth (30.42) in a Restricted WIN at this track. Solid record at the distance winning two races. Should bounce back. GUS THE GREAT (1) has some solid form under his belt and proved too strong last time to win by 3 lengths at Townsville in a handy 28.57 beating He's Peeking. Goes well out of this box with a win and two minor placings. Has definite claims. BALMAIN BOY (2) turned in a plain run last time when seventh at Capalaba over 366m behind Kachina Ripple (20.41) in a Grade 5. Good beginner aided by a nice draw. Better than last start and can bounce back. TUCKEROO ROAD (5) is worth including after a top-three finish in a tight contest most recently.",
